# Compute cost

Compute jobs that agents launch on machines other than their own (cloud VMs,
GPUs, clusters) share a cap of $10,000 a day in total (decision D8 in
`docs/template-plan.md`). There is no per-job limit. Each task states its
compute budget in US dollars, in the "Compute budget" section of its Linear
issue; a task that states none has a budget of $0.

Launch only with `mise run job:launch`, after reading the `compute-jobs`
skill. `mise run job:dry-run` prints a job's maximum cost. Stop to ask a
person, giving that estimate, if:

- any `mise run job:*` command says the compute client isn't installed,
  because until it is, nothing enforces the limits or the daily cap;
- the job would take the task's total compute spend, including failed runs,
  over its budget; or
- you can't estimate its cost.

Ask in the PR, and launch only after a person approves there. Never work
around a provider budget limit, for example by switching account or provider.
Never run `sky` directly, and never provision, change, or delete the compute
server unless a person asked for it in this task.
